meta {
  name: Create my profile
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/profile
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "username": "brunotester",
    "displayName": "Bruno Tester"
  }
}

docs {
  Completes onboarding. One-time: there is no rename endpoint yet.

  The username must be URL-safe, 3 to 30 characters, and not on the reserved list.
  That list has to include API-colliding tokens (`me`, `search`), which would
  otherwise shadow `GET /users/{username}`.

  Creating the profile also inserts both founder follow edges in the same
  transaction, so a new account never lands on empty lists.

  - 201 created
  - 403 signup cap reached (MAX_USERS)
  - 409 already has a profile, or the username is taken
  - 422 bad format or reserved
}
